From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Tue, 23 May 2023 11:15:31 +0100
Subject: brightsign: Add support for Brightsign video player

Adds compile and runtime options for Brightsign video player, which links
with libvid.

OS-18772: set visibility when video player is hidden with display none

When the video player is hidden (e.g. due to css display being set to none),
we need to set the visibility to hidden. This doesn't happen currently
because when its hidden we won't get a kVideoHole in the quad_list when
OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Propose is called. This will result in
no items being added to the candidates list, which in turn means that
OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Attempt will not be called. This patch
adds a check to see if the candidates list is empty and if so, sets the
visibility of the video player to hidden if last_factory_name_ is set.

OS-17206: fix video punch through with transparency

This patch fixes two issues related to video punch through with and without
transparency. The first issue was that we weren't searching through the render
pass list indexes in OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Propose in the same
way as done in OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Attempt. This was causing
Propose not to find VideoHoleDraw quads in the render pass list in some cases.
The second issue was causing issues when the punch through quad was drawn with
transparency. This has been fixed by using the correct blending mode when
replacing the quad with a solid color.

Fix overlay strategy for html pages with transparency OS-19250

Chromecast does not support overlays with opacity, so we need to
disable the opacity check in the overlay candidate factory. Additionally,
we need to fix the case when z-index is negative and we have VideoHoleDrawQuad
with transparency.

Brightsign fix overlay strategy for hwz on case OS-20978

This change restores BrightSign underlay behavior so handled VideoHoleDrawQuads
become true compositor holes and do not darken the primary plane when video opacity
is applied.

Background:

In the older QtWebEngine-based implementation, the BrightSign underlay path
effectively behaved like a side-effect-driven overlay strategy: it positioned the
external video plane and the compositor result matched the expected transparent-hole
behavior. In the newer Chromium overlay pipeline, BrightSign now participates in
the generic propose/attempt/commit overlay flow. In that newer flow, the handled
VideoHoleDrawQuad could still contribute visually in the non-negative z_index case,
which caused exposed video to not be blended correctly with the background, i.e
the primary plane of the HTML content.

Fix:

* Only propagate clip_rect into the copied shared quad state when the source quad is
actually clipped.
* Explicitly replace handled underlay VideoHoleDrawQuads with a transparent compositor
hole for the z_index >= 0 path.
* Keep the negative-z_index handling intact.
* Keep CommitCandidate() transparent so candidate commit does not reintroduce
destination darkening.
* Refactor the hole-punch logic into a local helper to keep the behavior centralized
and easier to reason about.

Brightsign fix overlay strategy for multiple render pass case
 OS-20978

The original implementation of VideoHoleDraw in overlay_strategy_underlay_brightsign.cc
had several issues when handling multiple render passes. We get into this scenario if an html
page has two or more video elements, which both have opacity less than 1.0.
In this case the code was only able to find the first referenced render pass, and then it
would stop searching for any more. This is because:
* It mutated the shared index while searching for a referenced render pass, which affects
subsequent traversal.
* It returned immediately after the first recursive success, so later aggregated quads in
the same quad list were never checked.
* It iterated over the full shared tokens list when inserting, instead of only the child
pass tokens.

The fix involves the following changes:
* Use local search_index instead of modifying index.
* Remove the early return after the first aggregated match.
* Recurse into each child pass with child_tokens and child_content_bounds, then merge
into parent outputs.
* Compose opacity through nesting as opacity * child_opacity.

